<item><title>WARNER RESERVE DOG OFF LEASH PARK</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Warner Reserve Dog Off-Leash Works include the redevelopment and expansion of the existing dog off-leash<br /><br />area to provide a fully enclosed, purpose-built dog park. The Works include the supply and installation of fencing<br /><br />to create separate All Dogs and Small Dogs areas, airlock entry gates, internal circulation paths, a central activity<br /><br />and seating node with park furniture, drinking fountain and shade structure, dog agility infrastructure, drainage<br /><br />improvements, planting works, mulching, signage, and all associated set-out, preparation, construction,<br /><br />reinstatement and incidental works necessary to deliver a complete, safe and functional dog off-leash facility.<br /><br />We are looking to award this tender by the end of December 2026 and for works to begin early 2027 with a provided calendar from suppliers.<br /><br />Delivery is Melbourne, Victoria - Australia.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> City of Greater Dandenong<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 20/Nov/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP531814<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation, Furniture & Furnishings, Horticulture & Arboriculture, Sport, Recreation Equip, Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 6]]></description>
