<item><title>Muswellbrook Marketplace UPSS Decommissioning Works</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Muswellbrook Shire Council is seeking tenders from suitably qualified, licensed and experienced contractors to permanently decommission the former underground petroleum storage system (UPSS) and underground LPG storage infrastructure at Muswellbrook Marketplace, 72–78 Brook Street, Muswellbrook NSW 2333. <br /><br />The preferred approach is permanent in-situ decommissioning because physical removal of the underground tanks is considered not reasonably practicable due to restricted access, excavation depth and the proximity of existing Marketplace structural elements. The works include petroleum product recovery, tank cleaning and gas-freeing, inert foam filling of petroleum USTs and associated pipework, specialist decommissioning and cementitious grout filling of the underground LPG vessel, removal of redundant above-ground fuel infrastructure and the oil/water separator, waste disposal, environmental validation and final decommissioning reporting.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Muswellbrook Shire Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 16/Nov/2026 10:00 AM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP531082<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation, Environmental & Heritage Services, Fuel & Oils<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 8]]></description>
