<item><title>201251 Depot Master Plan</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Sutherland Shire Council invites suitably qualified and experienced Lead Design Consultants to submit a Tender for the development of integrated Master Plans for four (4) key operational sites. The Master Plans will provide a coordinated, long-term strategic framework to guide the future use, development and management of Council's multidisciplinary operational facilities, ensuring they continue to meet current and future service delivery, workforce and community needs.<br /><br />This project encompasses Council's operational depots at Bath Road and Ethel Road, the Animal Shelter at Taren Point, and the Community Recycling Facility at Kurnell. The Master Plans will assess three (3) design options representing different scales of development: optimisation of existing facilities, redevelopment and consolidation of operations, and strategic transformation incorporating alternative sites or relocation opportunities.<br /><br />This Request for Tender (RFT) outlines the scope of services required from the Lead De...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Sutherland Shire Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 18/Nov/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP530369<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Architecture, Design, Planning, Business & Administrative Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 4]]></description>
