<item><title>Resource Recovery Education in Schools</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Council is seeking to engage a suitably experienced contractor to manage the delivery of resource recovery education incursion sessions to primary school groups within the Penrith Local Government Area. Currently Council contracts out 80 days worth of primary school resource recovery education sessions per year (20 days per term, 4-5 sessions/classes per day) and are looking to continue this arrangement. Council intends to enter into a 1-year agreement with the successful supplier.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Penrith City Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 13/Nov/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP531033<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Training & Development, Waste Management & Landfill<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 2]]></description>
