<item><title>ICT11010 Anatomical Pathology Specimen Tracking Solution</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The purpose of ICT11010 Anatomical Pathology Specimen Tracking Solution is to procure a fit-for-purpose software solution which provides the best value-for-money to meet the needs of Queensland Health.<br /><br />Anatomical Pathology (AP) has historically relied upon manual workflows which are at high risk of human error leading to potentially significant patient risk. In addition, automation and digital reporting are becoming available, both of which are reliant on modern IT systems to support their functioning. Implementation of an AP specimen tracking solution will improve patient safety, enable digital reporting, provide the IT connectivity for automation and improve overall productivity. <br /><br />The Customer has issued this Invitation to Offer with the objectives to:<br /><br />-	identify a fit-for-purpose solution which aligns to Queensland Health’s requirements<br /><br />-	derive the best value for money in accordance with Queensland Procurement Policy (QPP) targets and commitments and other relev...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> QH eHealth Queensland<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 04/Dec/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP530958<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Sam Mcmurchie Email: sam.mcmurchie@health.qld.gov.au Tel: 07 3542 6652<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : IT & Telecomms<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 4]]></description>
