<item><title>Expression of Interest - Southern Water Treatment Plant Project</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Toowoomba Regional Council (Council) is one of Queensland’s largest regional Councils, serving approximately 184,000 people across a geographical area of 12,973 square kilometres. Located in South East Queensland, approximately 125 kilometres west of Brisbane, the Region encompasses the city of Toowoomba, the regional centres of Oakey, Pittsworth, Millmerran, Highfields, Crows Nest, Clifton, Greenmount and Yarraman, and numerous smaller townships.<br /><br />Council is responsible for delivering and maintaining essential community infrastructure and services, including water, wastewater, waste, drainage, roads, bridges, footpaths, utilities and recreational facilities. Through its Water and Waste Services Group, Council manages the Region’s water treatment, storage and distribution assets, including the existing Mount Kynoch Water Treatment Plant (WTP).<br /><br />Water security is fundamental to supporting the continued growth and prosperity of the Toowoomba Region. The construction of the Queensland Governm...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Toowoomba Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 20/Nov/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP530840<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Water & Sewage<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 6]]></description>
