<item><title>Main Road Campbells Creek Tributaries – Flood Study</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Mount Alexander Shire Council ('Council') are seeking to engage a suitably qualified consultant to deliver and undertake a comprehensive flood study and develop conceptual design/s for flood mitigation solutions along Main Road (and adjacent tributaries) in Campbells Creek township.<br /><br />The successful consultant will provide specialist expertise in flood modelling, hydraulic and hydrologic assessment, climate change adaptation, planning and conceptual engineering design to improve understanding of flood behaviour within the Campbells Creek catchment, including the interaction between riverine flooding, stormwater runoff and tributary flows.<br /><br />The consultant will define the existing flood behaviour in the study area and the identification and evaluation of measures to mitigate and manage flood risk in the study area – including, but not limited to, recommendations for flood planning overlays, reviewing the performance of existing drainage, investigating potential mitigation works and updating e...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Mount Alexander Shire Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 20/Nov/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP530663<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Engineer, Research, Tech services, Environmental & Heritage Services, Management Advisory Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 5]]></description>
