<item><title>2027-034 Port to Mossman PCN</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> This project aims to engage a suitability qualified design consultant to undertake a planning assessment of the proposed construction and implementation of new off-road provisions for safe cycling between Port Douglas and Mossman in Far North Queensland. Douglas Shire Council and community have expressed an interest in repurposing the existing cane rail corridor between Port Douglas and Mossman Townships. The purpose of this planning works is to provide a clear path of what alignments are feasible, the condition state of the existing rail infrastructure proposed to be repurposed, costs and additional works required to position the council to seek or provide funding for additional stages including detailed design and ultimately construction of a new active transport path.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Douglas Shire Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 16/Nov/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP530643<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Engineer, Research, Tech services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 7]]></description>
