<item><title>Design of Taylor Bridge Replacement</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Scenic Rim Regional Council is situated in South-East Queensland, recognized for its stunning landscapes and vibrant communities. The Council is dedicated to enhancing the quality of life for residents and visitors through sustainable development and economic growth, partnering with reputable contractors to support ongoing projects.<br /><br />Council has received funding approval from the Australian Government under the Safer Local Roads and Infrastructure Program (the Program) to replace the existing timber bridge with a new concrete bridge with increased flood immunity. The new bridge and approximately 700m of Christmas Creek Road will be realigned to provide safe road geometry.<br /><br />As such Scenic Rim Regional Council (“Council” or “Principal”) is seeking tenders from suitably qualified suppliers for design services of the Taylor Bridge replacement.<br /><br />Design will include survey, geotechnical investigations, hydraulic assessment, environmental and cultural heritage assessments and detailed d...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Scenic Rim Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 12/Nov/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP528736<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Engineer, Research, Tech services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 8]]></description>
