<item><title>Regions for the Reef Program: Idea Exploration (Ideation phase)</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Office of the Great Barrier Reef and World Heritage (OGBR&WH) is seeking to procure the services of experienced suppliers with relevant regional knowledge, capability, and capacity to deliver the Regions for the Reef Ideation phase in one or more Reef sub-catchments. <br /><br />The supplier will create the space for diverse stakeholders across one or more Reef sub-catchments to come together and explore the potential opportunities and challenges in their local environment to – connect investment, resources and services; empower local communities; strengthen local economies; build an enduring legacy; and improve land management and Reef water quality outcomes. At the end of the project, the supplier will deliver a report to OGBR&WH on the outcomes of this collaboration and idea exploration process. <br /><br />OGBR&WH expects to fund multiple ideation initiatives to deliver collaborative forums and/or other engagement activities across the six Reef regions by the end of February 2027.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Dept of the Environ, Tourism, Science and Innov<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 19/Nov/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP530483<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Engineer, Research, Tech services, Environmental & Heritage Services, Event Management & Services, Management Advisory Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
