<item><title>ITT265 - IT Service Management</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Sunshine Coast Council is seeking to implement a modern, integrated ITSM platform to replace the current service management environment and provide a scalable foundation for improved technology service delivery. The project will initially focus on delivering a Minimum Viable Product (MVP) for core ITSM capabilities, including incident, request, change, problem, knowledge, service catalogue, service level management and reporting. The solution must also provide a clear pathway to expand into Enterprise Service Management (ESM), Software Asset Management (SAM), Configuration Management Database (CMDB) capability and controlled IT documentation management. The project is intended to improve service visibility, process consistency, user experience, operational reporting, asset and configuration intelligence, and Council’s ability to manage technology services in a controlled, sustainable and continuously improving manner.<br /><br />The objectives of this procurement are to:<br /><br />• Replace Council’s incumbe...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Sunshine Coast Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 12/Nov/2026 12:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP529822<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : IT & Telecomms<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 8]]></description>
