<item><title>Training Welding Bays and Fume Extraction Systems</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> TAFE Queensland is seeking information from suitably qualified suppliers regarding the provision of welding training bays, welding fume extraction systems, associated infrastructure, and supporting equipment for educational and training facilities across TAFE Queensland campuses.<br /><br />The information obtained through this RFI will assist TAFE Queensland in understanding available market capabilities, developing functional requirements, estimating budgetary considerations, and informing any future procurement strategy.<br /><br />TAFE Queensland encourages suppliers to propose innovative or emerging technologies that may provide superior welding fume control outcomes when compared to traditional local exhaust ventilation systems. Currently there are 26 identified campuses across the state that provide training requiring welding competencies. Solutions should be capable of supporting installations ranging from individual training bays through to larger multi-bay educational workshop environments.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> TAFE Queensland<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 06/Nov/2026 12:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP529541<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Indust. Production, Manufacturing, Mechanical Plant, Equip, Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 1]]></description>
