<item><title>Application Control</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Queensland Treasury seeks to procure and implement an enterprise-grade Application Control solution that enables organisation-wide enforcement of the ASD Essential Eight Application Control strategy across all supported endpoint and server platforms, as well as align with the Information Security Manual (ISM). <br /><br />The Customer has issued this Invitation to Offer with the objectives of achieving consistent application control enforcement across all endpoints and improved cyber resilience and compliance outcomes through sourcing a solution that will:<br /><br />•	Support achievement and maintenance of ASD Essential Eight Maturity Level 2 and Level 3 requirements.<br /><br />•	Provide application allowlisting and execution control.<br /><br />•	Reduce operational overhead associated with policy administration.<br /><br />•	Improve visibility, governance and reporting.<br /><br />•	Support Windows, macOS, Linux and server operating environments.<br /><br />•	Integrate with Treasury's broader endpoint secu...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Queensland Treasury<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 09/Nov/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP529765<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : IT & Telecomms<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 1]]></description>
