<item><title>RFT(EXC00136) Flood and River Level Monitoring Services for Townsville City Council</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Townsville City Council requires a vendor led solution under Stream B of the Enviromon Replacement project. The solution must replace the operational capability currently provided by Enviromon and TARDIS for the receipt, processing, storage, visualisation, alerting, reporting and onward distribution of flood warning observation data.<br /><br />Council currently relies on ALERT rainfall and water level gauge data to support disaster management, flood modelling, situational awareness and operational decision making across the Townsville Local Government Area. The Bureau of Meteorology has advised that support for Enviromon will cease in October 2026, and TARDIS is expected to reach end of support in 2027. The replacement solution must therefore provide a sustainable, secure and future ready capability that supports continuity of Council’s flood warning data operations before legacy support risks become unacceptable.<br /><br />The Supplier must provide a commercially available, configurable cloud SaaS solution...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Townsville City Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 12/Nov/2026 12:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP529325<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Engineer, Research, Tech services, IT & Telecomms, Utilities<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 5]]></description>
