<item><title>Supply of Kitchen Caddy Liners for Council&apos;s FOGO Collection Service</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Council is seeking a provider to supply and deliver kitchen caddy liners on an ongoing basis as required, as part of its new Food Organics Garden Organics (FOGO) collection service that will commence on 1 July 2027. <br /><br />Council will provide every household in the Blue Mountains Local Government Area (LGA) with a kitchen caddy that residents can use to place their food scraps in and carry them to their green kerbside FOGO bin. This caddy will be supplied with a pack of caddy liners that will help keep the caddy and green bin clean and make it easier for residents to transfer their food scraps from their caddy into their green bin.<br /><br />The caddy and the pack of liners supplied with it during rollout of the service will be provided by the FOGO collections contractor. This procurement is for the ongoing supply of liners that will be made available at Council sites and for delivery.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Blue Mountains City Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 03/Nov/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP528571<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Domestic & Consumer ELEC, Waste Management & Landfill<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 5]]></description>
