<pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Domestic &amp; Consumer ELEC</category>
<category>Waste Management &amp; Landfill</category>
</item>
<item><title>Request for Information - Transport Coordination Centre - Technology Capabilities</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Department of Transport and Main Roads (TMR) invites responses to this Request for Information (RFI) from suppliers of technology products, platforms, data, integration and related services that may support the Transport Coordination Centre (TCC).<br /><br />The Transport Coordination Centre (TCC) Program is a multi-year TMR transformation initiative to establish a statewide, integrated, multi-modal transport coordination facility and operating model. <br /><br />TMR will lead the TCC as a multi-modal operations centre that integrates Queensland’s key transport modes, including road, rail, bus, light rail and ferry. <br /><br />The TCC will oversee real-time network management, optimisation, disruption response, customer communications, demand management, data analysis and performance reporting. Its vision is to enable safer, smoother and more reliable travel for passengers and freight across Queensland through reduced travel times, improved journey reliability, faster incident response, personalised upda...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Department of Transport and Main Roads - ITB<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 13/Nov/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP529169<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : IT & Telecomms<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 1]]></description>
