<item><title>Wildlife Detection Technology</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Request for Information (RFI) – TMRICTRFI26178 Wildlife Detection Technology.<br /><br />TMR is seeking information on available and emerging solutions that support a range of capabilities associated with wildlife management in road environments. The capabilities are divided into four core pillars: Detection, Identification, Monitoring and Alerting. At a high level, TMR is interested in identifying technologies that can fully or partially support the four pillars:<br /><br />1. the automated detection of wildlife near the State Road Network.<br /><br />2. automated wildlife classification and identification. (accurate identification of wildlife species)<br /><br />3. automated monitoring of wildlife road-crossing activity and/or in proximity to road infrastructure.<br /><br />4. the automated generation of real-time alerts/notifications/warnings when wildlife is detected on or near road environments/corridors, together with reporting and analytics to support driver awareness.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Department of Transport and Main Roads - ITB<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 10/Nov/2026 04:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP528935<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : IT & Telecomms, Signs & Barriers<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 7]]></description>
