<item><title>CQURFQ-26-COMP10-DFM - Asbestos Register - Re-inspection</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> CQUniversity (CQU) invites quotes from suitably qualified and licensed contractors to undertake comprehensive re-inspections of asbestos-containing materials (ACM) across multiple CQU campuses. The purpose of this engagement is to verify the current condition of known and presumed ACMs, identify any previously unrecorded ACMs, assess associated risks, and provide updated ACM survey reports and asbestos register information for each site.<br /><br />Inspection and servicing must comply with all requirements of relevant Australian Standards, State and legislative requirements and industry best practices. The plan must be implemented with minimal disruption to campus operations, and all works must be performed to a standard that maintains compliance and achieves the agreed deliverables.<br /><br />The University's five-year review is due by the end of November 2026.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Central Queensland University<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 02/Nov/2026 04:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP528706<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation, Waste Management & Landfill<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 12]]></description>
