<category>Construction &amp; Operation</category>
<category>Waste Management &amp; Landfill</category>
</item>
<item><title>Pedestrian Operated Signals – Swan Hill</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Swan Hill Rural City Council (Council) is undertaking pedestrian safety improvements within the Swan Hill CBD through the installation of raised pedestrian operated signals at three key locations.<br /><br />The project forms part of Council’s program of infrastructure works and is intended to provide compliant pedestrian crossing infrastructure within busy urban areas. The works will be undertaken on existing road networks where maintaining safe access and minimising disruption to pedestrians, businesses, residents and road users will be important throughout construction.<br /><br />Due to the specialised nature of the works, delivery requires a suitably experienced and Department of Transport and Planning (DTP) accredited contractor, with all works to comply with relevant DTP/TAC standards and requirements.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Swan Hill Rural City Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 12/Nov/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP528647<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Construction & Operation, Fire & Safety, Parking, Traffic Services & Equip, Signs & Barriers<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 10]]></description>
