<item><title>Home Recycling Service</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Council is seeking a service provider to carry out collections of hard to recycle items from households as a separate home collection service in the Lane Cove Local Government Area (LGA). Items to be considered for acceptance include soft plastics, batteries, e-waste, small household electrical items, shoes, clothing, textiles, manchester, paint, blister packs, DVD’s, CD’s, and other tricky to recycle or problem wastes. Respondents are invited to include additional products that could be included in the collection for processing and reuse. Council has offered a collection service for problematic waste since August 2022. As of 1st July 2026, the service collects an average of 360 households per month and average annual collection of 45,000kgs.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Lane Cove Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 10/Nov/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP528205<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Ruby Gardiner Email: rgardiner@lanecove.nsw.gov.au Tel: (02) 9911 3657<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Waste Management & Landfill<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 1]]></description>
