<item><title>Cairns Marine Precinct - Common User Facility (CMP-CUF) Co-Investment</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Opportunity:<br /><br />Ports North is pleased to advise that Request for Proposal (RFP) Phase 1 for the Cairns Marine Precinct - Common User Facility (CMP-CUF) Co-Investment Opportunity has now commenced.<br /><br />Ports North is proposing the development of the Cairns Marine Precinct – Common User Facility, a major maritime infrastructure project, to expand the marine vessel maintenance capability and capacity in Far North Queensland to support the continued growth of the region’s maritime industry. The proposed facility responds to increasing demand for maritime maintenance, repair, and overhaul services as global vessel fleets expand and age, alongside sustained investment in Australia’s maritime defence capability driving long-term sustainment demand. <br /><br />Ports North has identified a Finance (co-funded), Design, Build, Operate and Maintain (FDBOM) commercial delivery model as the most efficient means of Project delivery to successfully facilitate achievement of the Project Objectives. As the...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Far North Queensland Ports Corporation Ltd<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 18/Dec/2026 12:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP526508<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation, ELEC, Lighting, Equip & Services, Engineer, Research, Tech services, Environmental & Heritage Services, Management Advisory Services, Marine Transp. Products & Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 0]]></description>
