<item><title>Call for Expressions of Interest: System Restart Service (SWIS-wide)</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> AEMO is seeking Expressions of Interest (EOI) to understand the availability, location and readiness of Facilities that may be able to provide System Restart Service across the SWIS. <br /><br /> <br /><br />Previous System Restart Service engagements have indicated that other existing or new Facilities may also be capable of providing System Restart Service, subject to necessary site works, testing and lead times. <br /><br />AEMO invites Market Participants, or prospective Market Participants, with Facilities capable of providing System Restart Service to make submissions for: <br /><br />* a Facility with System Restart Service capability to commence from 23 October 2028 (EOI Part 1); and <br /><br />* a Facility with System Restart Service capability to commence only after October 2030 (EOI Part 2). <br /><br />AEMO welcomes submissions for either existing or proposed Facilities with different technology configurations to submit an EOI. The EOI will be used by AEMO to determine the requirements of a subse...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Australian Energy Market Operator (AEMO)<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 09/Nov/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+08:00) Perth time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP524768<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Utilities<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 4]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/tsi.axd?id=0390ee8ab3e14cf5afefaf75e066b7b4s524768sc7f4c031498943fbb1aef808c6fbc4das2921</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">0390ee8ab3e14cf5afefaf75e066b7b4</guid>
<pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 03:36:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Utilities</category>
</item>
<item><title>ADVANCE TENDER NOTICE - Grounds Maintenance Services</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> ADVANCED TENDER NOTICE<br /><br />Grounds Maintenance Services (Group 4) – Preferred Supplier Arrangement<br /><br />The City of Moreton Bay (Council) provides prospective tenderers with an advance notice of its intent to invite Tenders to establish a Preferred Supplier Arrangement (PSA) for Grounds Maintenance Services. Moreton Bay City Council requires these Services, to support the operational needs of the city.<br /><br />The PSA would consist of a primary provider for each portion to perform scheduled maintenance in central and eastern districts.<br /><br />The purpose of this Vendor Panel (VP) event is an Advertisement only. There is no need to provide a response to this VP event or register your interest. For clarity a Close Date and Expected Decision Date are only listed due to being mandatory VP fields.<br /><br /><br /><br />TENDER DETAILS<br /><br />Council anticipates the Tender opportunity will be issued by a Request for Tender via VendorPanel in January 2027.<br /><br />Council will not accept a...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> City of Moreton Bay<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 31/Oct/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP524554<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Horticulture & Arboriculture<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 0]]></description>
