</item>
<item><title>Long-Term Reliability and System Strength Services for the North Country</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Reliability and System Strength Services for the North Country (Long-Term) - WS5659204351<br /><br />The Coordinator of Energy has determined, under clause 3.11A.4 of the Electricity System Market (ESM) Rules, to trigger a Non-Co-optimised Essential System Services (NCESS) procurement process by Western Power for Reliability and System Strength Services for the North Country.<br /><br />The proposed services aim to address reliability and system strength concerns during planned or unplanned outage events affecting one or more 132 kV transmission lines supplying the North Country.<br /><br />Call for NCESS Submissions<br /><br />Western Power invites NCESS Submissions from prospective NCESS providers to deliver Reliability Services and/or System Strength Services located in the North Country. The North Country is defined as the area supplied by the Rangeway, Geraldton and Chapman substations.<br /><br />This tender relates to the Long-Term contract term option (10-25 year terms). Proponents may offer a solutio...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Western Power<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 01/Feb/2027 05:00 PM (UTC+08:00) Perth time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP524329<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Peter Ling Email: peter.ling@westernpower.com.au Tel: 0893266185<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Utilities<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/tsi.axd?id=7574db831ebe4d6da73c79d1767d67f0s524329sc7f4c031498943fbb1aef808c6fbc4das2921</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">7574db831ebe4d6da73c79d1767d67f0</guid>
<pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 01:10:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Utilities</category>
</item>
<item><title>Palm Island Walking Trails &amp; Tourism Activation Project - Design &amp; Construct</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Palm Island Aboriginal Shire Council (Council) is seeking a suitably qualified and experienced Design & Construct (D&C) Contractor to undertake the design and construction of the Palm Island Walking Trails & Tourism Activation Project.<br /><br />The Project comprises the delivery of the walking trails, Cultural Welcome Precinct, eco accommodation / tourism accommodation base and associated tourism-supporting infrastructure described in Part B – Specification, including all investigations, surveys, assessments, design, approvals, construction, testing, commissioning, documentation and handover required to deliver the Works.<br /><br />The procurement is an implementation procurement based on the Project outcomes and recommendations identified in Part B. Tenderers are required to demonstrate the capability, capacity and methodology necessary to deliver the Works within Palm Island's remote-island, cultural, environmental and logistical context and achieve Practical Completion by 31 December 2027.<br /><br />Su...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Palm Island Aboriginal Shire Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 06/Nov/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP523582<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Marcio Fialho Email: marcio.fialho@palmcouncil.qld.gov.au Tel: 0448339292<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation, Signs & Barriers<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 28]]></description>
